@@ -0,0 +1,33 @@
+# Product review research
+
+## Request paths and data flow
+
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/api/v1/product/ProductReviewApi.java` handles public review reads, customer/admin review creation, updates, and deletes.
+- `ProductCommonFacadeImpl` converts API review models through `PersistableProductReviewPopulator`, then delegates persistence to `ProductReviewService`.
+- `ProductReviewRepository.findByProduct` eagerly joins the customer and product and is also used for duplicate detection through `findByProductAndCustomer`.
+- `ReadableProductReviewPopulator` currently calls `ReadableCustomerPopulator`, so the public response includes the entire readable customer model: email, billing/delivery addresses, attributes, groups, and other fields. This is the privacy leak.
+- The public response model `ReadableProductReview` inherits `productId` and exposes a `ReadableCustomer`; it is broader than the required review projection.
+
+## Causes found
+
+- Creation checks duplicate reviews and rating maximum manually, but sends HTTP 500 and 503 respectively instead of 409 and 400. The duplicate check also runs before replacing the request product id with the path id.
+- Bean validation has `@Min(1)` and `@Max(5)` on a `Double`, but no whole-number constraint. The endpoint therefore needs explicit whole-number validation (or an equivalent validation constraint) for ratings such as 4.5, while 9 currently reaches the wrong manual error path.
+- The customer POST trusts `customerId` from JSON. It does not compare it with the authenticated JWT customer id, allowing one customer to submit a review for another customer.
+- `PersistableProductReviewPopulator` always creates a new `ProductReviewDescription` set and does not merge an existing review. `ProductCommonFacadeImpl.saveOrUpdateReview` also always creates a new entity, even when an id is supplied.
+- `ProductReviewServiceImpl.saveOrUpdate` calculates a new average by adding the incoming rating and incrementing the count for both create and update. It never recalculates from the actual review rows. Delete only calls the generic repository delete and does not update product aggregates.
+- The product aggregate is stored on `Product.productReviewAvg` and `Product.productReviewCount`. The v2 `ReadableProductMapper` (and the minimal mapper) exposes these values, but rounds to half-star increments; the v2 product-by-SKU path uses `ProductFacadeV2Impl` and `ReadableProductMapper`.
+- The review update currently rejects a review when the body customer id differs, which is inappropriate for merchant administration and also requires customer data for an update. It does not verify that the review belongs to the path product before updating.
+- Update/delete path handling is in the same API class; missing reviews and product mismatches are already intended to be 404, but update currently lacks the product mismatch check.
+
+## Files likely affected
+
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/api/v1/product/ProductReviewApi.java`: status codes, authenticated customer ownership, path/product checks, and update/delete flow.
+- `sm-shop-model/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/model/catalog/product/ProductReviewEntity.java` and `ReadableProductReview.java`: validate whole ratings and narrow the public response shape.
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/populator/catalog/ReadableProductReviewPopulator.java`: copy only the review fields and reviewer first name.
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/facade/product/ProductCommonFacadeImpl.java` and `PersistableProductReviewPopulator.java`: merge existing reviews for merchant edits while preserving their identity and associations.
+- `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/services/catalog/product/review/ProductReviewServiceImpl.java`: recalculate product rating/count from persisted reviews after create, update, and delete, with one-decimal HALF_UP rounding and zeroes for no reviews.
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/mapper/catalog/product/ReadableProductMapper.java` and `ReadableMinimalProductMapper.java`: expose the stored one-decimal aggregate without half-star rounding.
+
+## Verification considerations
+
+- Existing integration coverage only creates a private review and does not cover the requested HTTP statuses, privacy shape, authenticated id checks, edit/delete aggregate changes, or v2 SKU output. Targeted tests or compilation plus the Maven test suites will be needed to catch these paths.
